   145	## 6. Bounding, Monte Carlo, and missingness rules
   146	
   147	### 6.1 Nuisance parameters
   148	
   149	- Every nuisance parameter must be registered by R4, **before** the estimator
   150	  is run, with an evidenced range or, absent evidence, its logical range.
   151	- **FEASIBLE / REQUIRES SEPARATE APPROVAL** determinations use the
   152	  least-favorable endpoint of every range jointly (the combination that
   153	  maximizes required resources). R4 must search the corners of the registered
   154	  box and any interior point its own validation shows can be worse.
   155	- **NOT FEASIBLE** determinations use the most-favorable endpoint of every
   156	  range jointly.
   157	- Central or "best-guess" values never decide a classification.
   158	- A range registered after the estimator has been run on decision inputs is
   159	  invalid (section 6.4).
   160	
   161	### 6.2 Supply bounds (from R2B)
   162	
   163	| Bound | Definition | Used for |
   164	|---|---|---|
   165	| `S_low` | Source clusters confirmed eligible under the frozen R3 rules, with complete provenance, minus R4's registered pilot reservation | FEASIBLE / REQUIRES SEPARATE APPROVAL |
   166	| `S_high` | `S_low` + pilot reservation + every cluster whose eligibility is missing, indeterminate, or unextracted because of tool/API/access failure; with pilot reservation 0 | NOT FEASIBLE |
   167	
   168	Clusters excluded for a recorded, rule-based cause are excluded from both
   169	bounds. Missing eligibility is **never** counted as ineligible (that would
   170	fabricate scarcity) and **never** counted as eligible for `S_low` (that would
   171	fabricate supply). The same rule applies to the number of distinct repository
   172	clusters. Historical and forward (future-horizon) supply are reported
   173	separately; R4 uses only historical supply unless R3/R2B freeze a forward
   174	estimate with its own bounds.
